\section{Form 8871 (\code{irs527})}{

68,365 rows over \strong{51,542 distinct EINs} - so the key is \code{FORM_ID_NUMBER}
(68,365 distinct, exactly the row count), not \code{EIN}. Each amendment is a new
row, which is why the file carries name variants at all: 1,231 EINs (2.4\%)
appear under more than one organisation name. Ingest is therefore
filing-level for \code{name}/\code{address} and deduplicated to EIN for \code{entity}.

EIN quality is perfect - all 68,365 are already bare 9-digit strings, none
blank. Notably better than \code{meta_names}, whose \code{EIN2} is \code{EIN-00-0019818}.

The file carries four address blocks (mailing, business, custodian, contact)
and two person-name fields. \code{CUSTODIAN_NAME} and \code{CONTACT_PERSON_NAME} are
legitimate \code{in_care_of} variants - an organisation genuinely written as
"c/o \if{html}{\out{<person>}}" is a spelling the matcher should know. \code{E_MAIL_ADDRESS}
should not be ingested: it carries no matching signal and is personal
contact data with no purpose in a disambiguation reference.
}

\section{Schedule R (\code{irs527_related})}{

62,153 rows over 8,377 EINs - only 16\% of 527s file one. Three findings
shape how it can be used, and two of them are restrictive:

\enumerate{
\item \strong{The related entity has no EIN.} The file gives
\verb{(527 EIN) -> (ENTITY_NAME, address)}. \code{ein_relation} as specified in
\code{PLAN.md} §4 is \verb{(ein_a, ein_b)}; this source cannot populate \code{ein_b}.
Resolving a name to an EIN is a matching problem, which is \code{npmatch}'s
job, not matchdb's - so these rows land with \code{ein_b} NULL and the
counterparty recorded by name, or they wait.
\item \strong{Most related entities are not nonprofits.} Only 1,102 of 10,597
distinct \code{ENTITY_NAME} values match a known 8871 organisation name -
about 10\%. The rest are sponsoring corporations, unions and trade
associations, largely outside the BMF universe entirely.
\item \strong{\code{ENTITY_RELATIONSHIP} is free text, not an enumeration.} 528
distinct values. \code{Connected} (54,660) and \code{Affiliated} (5,801) are 97.4\%
of rows, with a long tail running to \code{Mother}, \verb{Indirect Control} and
\verb{Common candidate-CA 33rd Assembly Dist.}. Any mapping onto the
\code{ein_relation.relation} enum has to be explicit and has to say what it
does with the tail.
}

Referential integrity to the 8871 file is close but not exact: 15,095 of
15,285 \code{FORM_ID_NUMBER} values resolve, leaving \strong{190 orphans (1.2\%)}.
}

\section{What must not happen}{

The related entity's name must never be registered as a \code{name} variant on the
527's EIN. \code{PLAN.md} §10 is explicit that affiliates are not DBAs, and this is
the case that most invites the error - "ASSOCIATION OF SAFETY GROUPS" is a
different body from "ASGM PAC", and aliasing them would manufacture exactly
the false matches the disambiguation database exists to prevent.
}

\section{An ingest hazard}{

\code{data.table::fread()} segfaults on the 8871 file; \code{utils::read.csv()} reads it
cleanly. The data is not malformed - line count and row count agree, so there
are no embedded newlines. Ingest should not assume \code{fread} on these.
}

